{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-12T10:56:52.209Z","author":"pi-vcs","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"b41e2b849c38c3f849ad0b06","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-12T10:56:52.209Z","author":"pi-vcs","text":"Verified the current state: setView's widening and narrowing already route every working-tree mutation through the shared WorktreeMutation boundary (WorktreeMutation.write/remove/prune), which PR 96 introduced and a later change on main applied to setView; no path-based rmSync/mkdirSync/writeFileSync/chmodSync remains in setView's apply loop. Re-confirmed the original reproduction is still real against the pre-boundary implementation: with only the setView apply loop reverted to the path-based version (rmSync/mkdirSync/writeFileSync/chmodSync), swapping the retained branch ancestor for an outside-directory symlink exactly at the widening write makes setView(null) succeed and the outside sentinel becomes the tracked bytes (content replaced, mode changed to 644 via the followed chmod). The fixed engine refuses the identical swap with worktree_path_changed and the sentinel stays byte-identical."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-12T10:56:52.209Z"}],"before_hash":"d285098f22c9358fdcb706d89d2d77c48b0f9073a6cded06f0f7aef0915b6fd9","after_hash":"0985e507f73b5d08f0b5276600b6cf05f497e31d0eabc07279d2546148176fe4","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d02a5f03b996971aadced4d344f9e958115ddab05d83a95788669635133ca10c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-12T10:57:14.876Z","author":"pi-vcs","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"b41e2b849c38c3f849ad0b06","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-12T10:57:14.876Z","author":"pi-vcs","text":"Added deterministic race tests in the shared worktree-races harness: setView narrowing (unlink), widening write (exclusive open) and widening mkdir each refuse ancestor replacement into both an outside directory and nested control state, across the pinned (between-steps and syscall boundaries) and portable (with and without O_NOFOLLOW) strategies — 24 tests, all passing. Injections reuse the same seam as the PR 96 race tests (fs syscall hooks plus the lstat observation boundary; the shared intercept helper gained an explicit observation override for the sparse-preflow shift). Each test asserts the typed worktree_path_changed refusal, byte-identical outside sentinels with unchanged modes, and that the recorded view and index are untouched by the refusal."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-12T10:57:14.876Z"}],"before_hash":"0985e507f73b5d08f0b5276600b6cf05f497e31d0eabc07279d2546148176fe4","after_hash":"0101ec8f4a35cfab42bb97e5ba010767156f01aa0a0dd6094072a8a4368a6ba8","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a6b974be1c79eeb846ee0855194d16fd4796c407128cfd69b56185df889137c2"}
